/T (In the face of a life-threatening illness like cancer, the journey of treatment often focuses heavily on medical interventions and survival. However, amid the tests, treatments, and hospital visits, an equally vital need often goes unnoticed: the need for relief from pain, emotional distress, and spiritual suffering. This is where palliative care steps in.)
/E (In the face of a life-threatening illness like cancer, the journey of treatment often focuses heavily on medical interventions and survival. However, amid the tests, treatments, and hospital visits, an equally vital need often goes unnoticed: the need for relief from pain, emotional distress, and spiritual suffering. This is where palliative care steps in.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Palliative care is a specialized approach that aims to improve the quality of life for patients and their families by addressing the physical, emotional, social, and spiritual challenges of serious illnesses. Unlike curative treatments that target the disease itself, palliative care focuses on the person, offering relief from symptoms such as pain, fatigue, breathlessness, nausea, anxiety, and depression.)
/E (Palliative care is a specialized approach that aims to improve the quality of life for patients and their families by addressing the physical, emotional, social, and spiritual challenges of serious illnesses. Unlike curative treatments that target the disease itself, palliative care focuses on the person, offering relief from symptoms such as pain, fatigue, breathlessness, nausea, anxiety, and depression.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In cancer care, palliative services are not just for those nearing the end of life. They are most effective when introduced early in the disease trajectory, alongside curative or life-prolonging treatments. Studies have shown that early palliative care can improve patient outcomes, enhance emotional well-being, and even extend survival.)
/E (In cancer care, palliative services are not just for those nearing the end of life. They are most effective when introduced early in the disease trajectory, alongside curative or life-prolonging treatments. Studies have shown that early palliative care can improve patient outcomes, enhance emotional well-being, and even extend survival.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
